# Root-level secrets written by the Neon CLI (neon link / neon config) —
# contains live database and object-storage credentials, never commit.
.env.local
.env
.env.*.local

# .neon holds only non-secret IDs (org/project/branch) — safe to commit,
# listed here only so it's not missed if that ever changes upstream.
.mcp.json

# Google Cloud Console's raw OAuth client-secret download — contains a
# real client_secret credential, never commit it. The app itself never
# reads this file (Google ID-token verification only needs the client
# ID for audience checks, not the secret) — it's a leftover download
# from OAuth setup, safe to keep locally but never in version control.
client_secret_*.json
